findings.evidence:
Doc :30-34: 'Every Saha result is stated for one ionization energy χ. An IPD-lowered χ − Δχ is fine, provided forward and inverse use the same value.' The rows it offers as acceptance criteria all quantify over T at a fixed χ: sahaFactor_strictMonoOn_temp (:62), electronDensityFromRatio_strictMonoOn_temp (:56), sahaFactor_lipschitz_temp (:61), electronDensityFromRatio_mem_Icc (:67) and outerLoop_contracts_apriori (:68). Several also need hEχ : ∀ k, EZ k ≤ chi.
With Debye-Hückel IPD (partition.py:81-95) the effective χ varies with T and n_e, which breaks this in three ways:
(i) the T-grid rows do not apply;
(ii) R·n_e = S(T, χ − Δχ(n_e)) is a fixed-point equation, not the explicit ↔ of saha_relation (:53);
(iii) the pipeline's cutoff Eᵢ < IP − Δχ (partition.py:207) changes the level list, so U jumps as (n_e, T) cross thresholds. partitionFunction_lipschitz_temp (:64) cannot hold across a jump.
The doc's own row at :18 warns that 'a clamped, tabulated or polynomial U' breaks these rows, but it does not extend that warning to the IPD cutoff. The overhaul records the IPD-on inverse as an inner n_e fixed point: R9-performance.md:36, 'With apply_ipd=True, IP_eff(n_e,T) adds a 1-D inner n_e fixed point'. Ristić 2024 (DOI 10.1088/1361-6587/ad8b68) shows the partition-function correction dominates at high T.

CompositionRobustness.lean:13-37 calls the chain 'the per-element reliability deliverable for many-element alloys', with hypothesis hdelta : ∀ s, |Nhat s − N s| ≤ delta (one δ for all species). classicComposition_atomicData_error (:295) assumes a RELATIVE response error δ but feeds Nmax·(δ/(1−δ)) into composition_abs_sub_le_bound. noise_to_composition (:281) does the same with Nmax·Φ. C6 (Certificates.lean:206-211) certifies one absolute tolerance τ_C for every species.
Numerical check: N = (0.995, 0.005), 5% multiplicative error, worst case over sign patterns:
- actual |ΔC_minor| = 5.23e-4 (10.5% relative);
- exact multiplicative bound 2δ/(1−δ)·C = 5.26e-4;
- repo bound compositionErrorBound N Ŝ (Nmax·δ/(1−δ)) = 0.0557, which is 11 times the minor fraction itself and 106 times too loose.
Literature (retrieved): Gornushkin & Völker 2022, 'Intrinsic Performance of Monte Carlo Calibration-Free Algorithm for LIBS', Sensors 22:7149, DOI 10.3390/s22197149: 'small errors at high concentrations are transformed into large errors at low concentrations. This disadvantage, however, is not inherent in single-point calibration methods that do not use such summation'. Overhaul R11-05 builds its ratio-mode proposal on this claim.

MatrixEffects.lean:61-62: 'Borduchi, L. C. L.; Milori, D. M. B. P.; Villas-Boas, P. R. Spectrochimica Acta Part B (2022)'. Semantic Scholar (bord.json) has two candidates:
- the 2022 paper, 'Reducing matrix effects on the quantification of Ca, Mg, and Fe in soybean leaf samples using calibration-free LIBS and one-point calibration', by Borduchi, Milori, M. C. Meyer, Villas-Boas, SAB, DOI 10.1016/j.sab.2022.106561;
- the three-author paper, 'One-point calibration of Saha-Boltzmann plot to improve accuracy and precision…', SAB 2019, DOI 10.1016/j.sab.2019.105692.

DifferentialEstimator.lean:67-69: 'one reference sample of known composition … exactly as one-point-calibration (OPC) schemes do'. Its only prior art is stellar (:78-87: Meléndez 2009, Bedell 2014, Nissen & Gustafsson 2018). Its EXACT rows cite 'Ciucci 1999', and the REDUCED bound cites 'Aguilera & Aragón 2007' (scope-tags.tsv:643-653).
Retrieved:
- Cavalcanti, Teixeira, Legnaioli, Lorenzetti, Pardini, Palleschi 2013, 'One-point calibration for calibration-free LIBS quantitative analysis', SAB, DOI 10.1016/J.SAB.2013.05.016 (99 citations);
- Borduchi et al. 2019, DOI 10.1016/j.sab.2019.105692;
- Hu et al. 2022, Opt. Lett., DOI 10.1364/ol.472224 (self-absorption correction plus OPC).
Pipeline: opc.py:14-24 cites Cavalcanti 2013. It 'fixes the plasma temperature at the mean of the selected standards' optimal T*' and derives 'one robust per-element relative-sensitivity factor F by the geometric mean of C_true/C_rec'. That is a per-element factor at a pooled T. differentialComposition_exact_of_matched instead needs per-line ratios at a matched T.

